  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened policies for decent work in the digital economy and for sustainable and responsible enterprises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Country Programme Outcome (CPO) supports Brazil in advancing a coherent policy framework that aligns economic development with social justice in the context of accelerating digital transformation and persistent labour market challenges, including informality and inequality. Emphasis is placed on promoting Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work (FPRW), strengthening responsible business conduct, and ensuring inclusive governance of digitalization through social dialogue and evidence-based policymaking.

The expected outputs include the development and implementation of a National Human Rights and Business policy aligned with international labour standards, alongside strengthened tripartite dialogue through national platforms such as the National Forum on Human Rights and Business. In parallel, a comprehensive, tripartite-validated assessment of the impacts of digitalization on jobs, enterprises, and skills will inform integrated policy responses. These efforts are expected to enhance national capacities to promote sustainable and responsible enterprises and to design strategies for decent work in the digital economy, contributing to more resilient, inclusive labour markets and improved job quality.</narrative>
  </description>
